// bubbler profile: lutris
//
// Lutris itself is a GTK app, but every Wine or Proton game it starts is
// an X11 client — Wine's X11 driver takes precedence over its Wayland one
// whenever DISPLAY is set (Arch wiki, Wine#Wayland) — so this profile
// grants `x11`, with the isolation caveat that carries: X11 clients can
// keylog and inject into each other.
//
// `seccomp { disable }` is here for the same reason as in `steam`: umu,
// Proton and DXVK's 32-bit path make i386 syscalls, and the filter holds
// one architecture. Never add `userns "disable"` either — those runtimes
// nest pressure-vessel's own bubblewrap.
//
// GameMode is optional on the host: the D-Bus name below simply resolves
// to nothing when gamemoded is not installed.
//
// `portals` stays because Lutris calls them itself. Not measured here: a
// Proton or umu game brings pressure-vessel, the same steam-runtime-tools
// that refuses to run where /.flatpak-info exists (see `steam`), so drop
// the grant if a game stops with a Flatpak complaint.
//
// ~/Games is Lutris's own convention for the install directory, and a
// missing share source is an error rather than a skipped bind, so create
// it (`mkdir ~/Games`) or edit the node to the directory you use. A prefix
// or library outside the home is named explicitly, e.g.
//   path-share "/kioxia/Games" mode=rw
wayland
x11
dri
pipewire
network
dbus {
    own "net.lutris.Lutris"
    talk "com.feralinteractive.GameMode"
    talk "org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver"
}
portals
notify
tray
gamepad
system-bus {
    talk "org.freedesktop.UDisks2"
}
home-share "Games" mode=rw
seccomp {
    disable
}
command "lutris"
